hello everyone peter brown here with a  gamespot news update dice has just  informed us that battlefield hardline  has been delayed until 2015 the vp and  group GM of dice released a statement on  the battlefield blog explaining their  reasons for the unexpected delay  according to the statement feedback that  the developer received during the beta  has caused them to start thinking about  other possibilities in ways they could  push hard line innovation further and  make the game even better but in order  to do so dice said it needs more time  the statement lists three improvements  that the company hopes to implement with  the extra time the first is multiplayer  innovation including ideas direct from  the community that will evolve the cops  and criminals fantasy into a truly  unique battlefield multiplayer  experience dice also wants to flush out  the single-player story including  polishing the core features as well as  adding new ones that will support a  deeper crime revenge story experience  and finally the team wants to improve  stability saying that they have learned  a lot from battlefield 4 and will  continue to learn from another hardline  beta the extra time will allow them to  fix more issues before launch the  statement also mentions that dice  continues to work on battlefield 4 the  dragon's teeth DLC is coming out July 29  with more DLC plan for later in the year  no word yet on the adjusted release date  other than early 2015 but for more  information on battlefield stay tuned to  gamespot com
 

